# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# This repository accompanies a manuscript under review. It publishes the
# evaluation harness, its result records, and the engine source — and nothing
# else. Everything is excluded by rule, then re-admitted explicitly, because
# the working tree also holds 2.9 GB of derived corpus features that the
# paper's Data Availability statement says are NOT redistributed.
#
# To publish something new, add an explicit un-ignore. Do not relax `/*`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*

# ── Published ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/INSTALL.md
!/ComparisonResults
!/layer2
!/project
!/tests
!/.clang-format
!/.clang-tidy
!/.editorconfig
!/.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ── datasets/: the README only; never the derived feature tree ───────────────
!/datasets
/datasets/*
!/datasets/README.md

# ── project/: source only; build/ is a regenerable Meson dir whose
#    compile_commands.json embeds absolute developer paths (91 occurrences).
#    `make` recreates it from meson.build.
/project/build/

# ── Never published, and why ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# academic-research-skills/  vendored tooling, unrelated to this study
# jcp_paper/                 manuscript sources, build artefacts, backups
# local tool state          editor and assistant caches, unrelated to this study
# datasets/extracted/        2.9 GB derived corpus features (see above)

# ── Regenerable / local noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
*.log
*.aux
*.out
*.bak
*.pre_*
*.tmp
.DS_Store

# build artifacts must never reach the deposit
*.so
*.o
**/__pycache__/
